{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3449","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3449","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3449\",\"parent_revision\":\"e60b244abe94ee8e3f7fe9086390aabea0c9eaf2\",\"root_revision\":\"aff40ed0f50dc14adbb352991bd20b3abf318467abbb79be751ca70110c8b283\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nTracks the architecture and slice plan in `plugins/development-harness/docs/work-ledger.md` (landing on `worktree-melodic-plotting-emerson`). The plan replaces the plan content record, the active-task record, the session-id capture hook, the SubagentStop adjudication, the dispatch-plan schema, `dispatch-state.db` and the kage-bunshin session registry with one local SQLite ledger per project, keyed by task address, with a lease as the only runner key, and one work loop: dispatch, run, finish, judge against the task's acceptance criteria, then accept or send back with a response, bounded by attempts, until the plan is satisfied.\\n\\nWHY\\n\\nVerified against the code on 2026-09-06 (file:line in the document):\\n\\n- Both SAM frontends store a plan as one JSON content record with a revision compare-and-swap (`ContentTaskProvider`). Two runners mutating different tasks of one plan collide; `claim_task` reports the collision as \\\"already claimed\\\". Every write is a remote round trip on the GitHub backend, including the PostToolUse `last-activity` update; every CLI process pages every plan record first.\\n- The SubagentStop hook attributes a stop through an active-task record keyed by a session id every sub-agent shares (#3431) and writes task state from the worker's return text.\\n- The milestone path's spawn invocation and `_build_spawn_cmd` both pass flags `spawn.py`'s parser rejects; `dispatch-state.db` is built outside `DH_STATE_HOME`; two orphan hook files are registered nowhere.\\n- No orchestrator step judges a finished task against its acceptance criteria and sends it back, so unsatisfying results are accepted or repaired by hand.\\n\\nSLICES (one PR each, each with a red-then-green test named in the document)\\n\\n0 measure (M1 hook payload, M2 consumer grep, M3 store census, M4 Codex payload, M5 live-run CI, M6 worktree sub-agents) \u00b7 1 ADRs (identity and lease; the ledger; the work loop; one dispatch path; remotes as projections; supersedes ADR-1770-1 on two points) \u00b7 2 ledger module and `sam plan` commands with tests under `tests_sam/` \u00b7 3 MCP parity \u00b7 4 the work loop in `dispatch`, `implement-feature`, `multi-perspective-review`, `complete-implementation`, the runner contract, hooks as accelerators, deletions \u00b7 5 milestones on the same path, kage-bunshin retired \u00b7 6 content record retired as a store \u00b7 7 projection checks \u00b7 8 documentation.\\n\\nRelated: #3431 (correlation key, superseded by the lease), #3432 (`_default` sentinel, disappears with the active-task record), #3433 (reaping, becomes lease expiry), #3445 (scanner exemption, unrelated to storage), #3429 and #3430 (moot once the shared doc and the active-task record are gone).\\n\\nM3 machines: to be listed here during grooming.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Design session 0123saEQFTYnFb79CLozrH7i, 2026-09-06, after the review of PR #3427 and the plan \\\"DH work-tracking: key on the work item, not on the runner\\\"\\n- **Priority**: P0\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: M1, M4, M5, M6 in the document\\n</div>\\n\\n## Work Brief Extension Durable Non Complete Attempt Disposition 2026 09 24\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-24T04:40:02.370632Z</sub>\\n\\n## Desired outcome\\n\\nEvery failed, blocked, or needs-input attempt in the DH work loop must durably record absent outputs, the observed reason, and exactly one current disposition: `retrying`, `awaiting user`, `repairing blocker`, `backlogged`, or `accepted as terminal`. The disposition must be queryable by the next orchestrator or judge so the attempt cannot remain as an unconsumed note with no next action. A changed disposition supersedes the prior current disposition through the ledger's event history rather than erasing it.\\n\\n## Observed gap and evidence\\n\\n#3449 already owns the event-sourced ledger and dispatch-run-finish-judge loop. The targeted preflight found no required outcome vocabulary or durable disposition for every non-complete attempt; present note consumption is manual through judge/reclaim.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\nA failed or blocked worker can leave durable observations without a durable decision about retry, user input, repair, backlog transfer, or terminal acceptance. Later actors must reconstruct intent and may repeat work or silently abandon it.\\n\\n## Scope boundaries\\n\\n#3449 remains the sole work-loop and ledger owner. #3099 remains the declared failure-policy input and #3102 remains the attempt-counter input. This extension does not replace either issue, prescribe a new retry policy, or merge domain verdicts with transport status.\\n\\n## Readiness and acceptance conditions\\n\\nEvery non-complete attempt must expose its absent outputs, reason, and one allowed current disposition. The loop must prevent a non-complete attempt from reaching an unaccounted terminal state, while preserving its event history and the separate policies and counters supplied by related owners.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"f4b8ac67561ffccb6e053460e39f1562c5a9cbd8c2ed8a1485c07d0333c7eefe\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABWiwMzA\"}"}